<div class="phead"><div class="w"><ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="{{ PathBase }}/">Halvorsen 2027</a></li><li>Meet Noor</li></ol><p class="kick">Meet Noor</p><h1>Fourteen years on county roads</h1><p class="lede">Noor Halvorsen was the Wrenfield County extension agent from 2011 to 2025. She lives in Ashby Ford with her husband, two teenagers and an unreasonable number of tomato plants.</p></div></div><section class="sec tight"><div class="w"><div class="dg"><div class="prose"><p>For fourteen years my job was to drive to farms, schools and church basements across the county and help people solve practical problems: soil tests, 4-H, food safety classes, a well that went bad. I learned where every bad bridge is because I had to drive around them.</p><p>I am running for the District 2 seat because most of what people asked me for over those years was not something the extension office could fix. It was a bridge, a clinic hour, a meeting held when they could come. Those are county commission decisions.</p><p>The seat is nonpartisan, and I am running without a party endorsement. I will tell you exactly how I would vote on the commission, item by item, and it is on this site.</p><h2>What I will not do</h2><ul><li>Take contributions from vendors who do business with the county.</li><li>Vote on a budget that has not been online for thirty days.</li><li>Promise a date I cannot explain.</li></ul></div><aside><ol class="vtl"><li class="past"><span class="when">1982</span><b>Born in Quillon</b><p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0">Mill village, second-shift family.</p></li><li class="past"><span class="when">2004</span><b>Agronomy degree, state university</b></li><li class="past"><span class="when">2011 – 2025</span><b>County extension agent</b><p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0">Farm roads, 4-H, food safety, soil and wells.</p></li><li class="past"><span class="when">Sep 2026</span><b>Campaign launch at the Ashby Ford bandstand</b></li><li class="vote"><span class="when">Apr 6, 2027</span><b>Election Day</b></li></ol></aside></div></div></section>
